## This tree is a DEPLOY TARGET
`~/.claude` deploys from `<your-org>/<your-private-harness>`. Edit in `~/your-private-harness`, commit, push, run `~/.claude/scripts/gearbox deploy`. Never commit, force-push, or `--no-verify` here. `~/.codex/skills` is a second deploy target: edit `skills/<name>/codex/`, let `gearbox deploy` render it, and never hand-edit or hand-copy a file there.

- **Runtime output** (`projects/*/memory/**`, `_plans/**`, routing eval output, binary-rewritten `settings.json` keys: `model`, `effortLevel`, `permissions.allow`) is harvested by `gearbox deploy`; other new files (results, `_evidence/`, >=200 KB) need `~/.claude/scripts/gearbox harvest`.
- **Other edits here are hotfixes** (`hooks`, `env`, `permissions.deny` in `settings.json`): `gearbox deploy` refuses until `gearbox drift` and `gearbox harvest` carry them back.
- **Codex render:** run `scripts/render-codex-instructions.py` after editing `CLAUDE.md` or `rules/*.md` (Claude-only text in `<!-- claude-only -->`; never edit `codex/global-instructions.md`).
- `~/Gearbox` is public export, never source (`README.md`, `scripts/deploy.pathspec`).

